---
import source from '../../../example/src/main.rs?raw';
import manifest from '../../../example/Cargo.toml?raw';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Complete consumer example — gpui-agentation</title><meta name="description" content="A complete minimal GPUI app with native Agentation annotations, assets, keyboard focus, and debug guards."><link rel="icon" href={`${base}assets/mark.svg`}><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}styles.css`}></head>
<body><header class="header wrap example-header"><a class="brand" href={base}><img src={`${base}assets/mark.svg`} alt="" width="27" height="27">gpui-agentation</a><nav aria-label="Example navigation"><a href={`${base}#setup`}>Back to setup</a></nav></header><main class="wrap" style="max-width:880px;padding-top:60px"><section class="doc-section"><h1 style="font-size:38px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-1.5px">A complete consumer app.</h1><p>A minimal native window, one selectable component, and a retained annotation overlay. This uses the published <code>gpui-agentation =0.3.0</code> API and keeps native annotation integration behind debug guards.</p><p>Create the two files below in a new directory, then run <code>cargo run</code>. A native GPUI toolchain is required; this example was checked on macOS in debug and release configurations.</p><p><a class="button" href="Cargo.toml" download="Cargo.toml">Download Cargo.toml</a> <a class="button" href="src/main.rs" download="main.rs">Download main.rs</a></p><p class="small-note">Place <code>main.rs</code> inside <code>src/</code>. The app stores local feedback under <code>target/agentation/</code> and listens on port <code>4748</code>. Run one process per store file. In release mode there is no annotation overlay or listener.</p><div class="code-block"><div class="code-header">Cargo.toml</div><pre><code>{manifest}</code></pre></div><div class="code-block"><div class="code-header">src/main.rs</div><pre><code>{source}</code></pre></div><p><a class="inline-link" href={`${base}#mcp`}>Next: connect your MCP client →</a></p></section></main></body></html>
